# Project Instructions — <REPO> (lite mode)

This Project uses **lite mode** of the claude_researcher workflow
(`github.com/danparshall/claude_researcher`, `template_lite/`) — for small
utility repos that don't need the full research machinery.

## Credentials

```bash
TOKEN="<TOKEN>"
USER=<USERNAME>
REPO=<REPO>
```

`<TOKEN>` is a fine-grained GitHub PAT scoped to read/write `<USERNAME>/<REPO>`
(possibly among other repos). Don't echo it to the user or write it into any
repo file — it's a scoped, rotatable credential designed to live in this
Project Instructions context.

## Session start

Clone the repo, then read `LITE.md` at its root — that file is the runtime
spec (memory model, disposition, session-end rules) and takes precedence over
anything here except the credentials:

```bash
git clone --depth 1 "https://x-access-token:${TOKEN}@github.com/${USER}/${REPO}.git" /home/claude/${REPO}
```

Do this before any other tool calls that touch the user's repos. Don't call
`conversation_search` / `recent_chats` at session start — `STATUS.md`,
`DECISIONS.md`, and `git log` are the record.

If anything looks inconsistent with the user's actual setup (wrong username,
wrong repo, expired token), stop and surface the mismatch before doing work.
